# Vault status when picking up work

**Before** writing code, dispatching an implementer, or starting **any** vault card: set that card's `status: In progress` and **commit it**. The board must show In progress while an implementer owns the tree.

- One current **implementer** card: `In progress` before dispatch.
- When the implementer has committed: parent sets `In review` and **commit**, then dispatch the task reviewer. Pickup of the next `Not started` card is allowed (reviewer is read-only).
- Implementer must **not** set `Done` or `In review`. `Done` only after the reviewer is **Approved** (or no review for a status-only/wiki-only change). Then `Done` + Resolution in that commit.
- Needs fixes → back to `In progress` (not a separate status).
- `Blocked`: stop pickup; write why in the card body (question to the human, missing asset, open dependency).
- When `current: true` moves to a new sprint, update the **Current sprint** view filter in `vault/production/Task board.base` (`sprint == "Sprint N"`).

Do not skip this because the slice is “small” or the subagent will flip Done later.
